@thecoldbelow I feel you.  One of my boys had a new teacher once who was a bit shouty.  That evening he spent hours in meltdown.  He was inconsolable.  I stayed with him in his room and held him (he is a very cuddly boy) but it did take hours.  We talked about the new teacher the next day and I communicated what had happened to the school.  

It does make you feel helpless when you are waiting for them to calm down.  Being stressed yourself though won’t help at all. 

I do agree with the video though that if nothing works we should seek help.  Help won’t hurt!

@japko8867 In Shinto, there is a belief that God dwells in all things. This applies to even a single grain of rice.
Many Japanese are aware that it is bad manners to leave a grain of rice on the table.
As a Japanese, I can understand why they would want to point this out. However, I also understand that it is a way of thinking that is not understood.
